//RS     // NOT a supported mode, so this helper refuses it by name instead of
//RS     // letting it fail 10,000 lines deep in someone else's fragment.
//RS     //
//RS     // `--test` asks rustc to synthesize a harness from every `#[cfg(test)]`
//RS     // module in the crate. The generated crate is one flat splice of the
//RS     // Prelude, so that switch activates the COMPILER's private fragment unit
//RS     // tests inside a user program — a set that is not the program's tests, is
//RS     // not shipped, and whose only shared namespace is the generated crate root.
//RS     // The supported way to run Jet tests is `jet test`, which builds its own
//RS     // harness (TEST_PRELUDE / `jet_test_print`). A probe that needs to observe
//RS     // generated internals hooks the generated `main` instead — see
